---

pick a theme with `"theme"` in `assets/notizine.ziggy`:

- `nord-default` - nord palette on the standard skeleton, the starter's
  default
- `everforest-default` - same skeleton in everforest colors: warm cream
  light mode, deep green-grey dark mode
- `sccl` - one centered window on a flat backdrop, space mono,
  nord-inspired palette (this site uses it... well, used to)
- `motherfuckingwebsite` - barely any css: system serif, single column,
  default link colors. 4kb of styling total. want a catgirl pink theme
  instead? it's just tokens, go wild

# tokens

themes are thin layers over the same css custom properties:

```css
:root {
  --bg: #2e3440;         /* page backdrop */
  --accent: #88c0d0;     /* links, highlights */
  --page-width: min(70vw, 55rem);
  /* ...borders, code background, tag colors, fonts... */
}
```

override any of them via `custom_css` - point it at a file in `assets/`
and it gets appended after the theme, before purging.

# fonts

no css needed for type: set `fonts.heading`, `fonts.body` or
`fonts.code` to any font-family value, or use `google_fonts` with a
query string like `"Inter:wght@400;700"`.

# gotchas

css is purged at build time - selectors that never appear in the final
html get removed. if your custom styles target classes that only exist
inside module output, make sure that module is actually slotted in, or
the rules will be stripped.
